cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Minimum Sufficient Compute (MSC)"
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bonal
    given-names: Shanmukesh
repository-code: "https://github.com/NewUser4622/minimum-sufficient-compute"
abstract: >-
  Per-sample, cost-normalised measurement of the compute a trained network
  needs, and an analysis of oracle upper bounds for early-exit inference.
  Any-correct-exit oracle accuracy exceeds final-exit accuracy
  (+6.86 pt median on the CIFAR-100 atlas, evaluated over 90 ordered seed
  pairs from 45 models; +7.39 and +6.91 pt on a custom ImageNet-100 subset;
  +7.74 and +7.91 pt in two seeds of a documented MSDNet variant).
  The project studies complementary exit predictions, seed-transfer policies,
  and budget-dependent comparisons with practical early-exit rules.
keywords:
  - early exit
  - adaptive inference
  - example difficulty
  - oracle bounds
license: MIT
